  "scope": [
    "Module TIM as delivered by ST (STM32CubeN6 v1.4.0), FROZEN: the TIM HAL component (classic, handle-based) and the TIM LL component (header-only inline functions) under one functional-level requirement set, for the general-purpose timers TIM2/TIM3/TIM4/TIM5 (RM0486 chapter 54). The delivered HAL does not use the delivered LL: the two components are parallel public APIs over the same peripheral.",
    "In scope (HAL): time base, output compare, PWM, input capture, one-pulse and encoder interface modes, each with initialisation and de-initialisation, platform hooks, channel configuration, blocking, interrupt-driven and DMA-driven start and stop, and state queries; clock source selection; slave-mode and master-mode synchronisation; interrupt handling and software event generation; captured value read-back; callback registration and unregistration and the period-elapsed, compare, capture, pulse-finished, trigger, error and half-complete callbacks; active channel and channel state queries.",
    "In scope (LL): counter enable; time-base configuration (update event and source, one-pulse, counter mode, auto-reload preload, clock division, counter, direction, prescaler, auto-reload); capture/compare channel control; output compare configuration and compare values of channels 1 to 4; input capture configuration and captured values of channels 1 to 4; clock source, encoder mode, trigger output, slave mode, trigger input, master/slave mode and external trigger configuration; DMA requests, interrupts, status flags and event generation for update, channels 1 to 4 and trigger.",
    "Out of scope (delivered; listed by the governance inventory): the vendor-internal helper functions the delivered HAL headers declare, the HAL DMA burst services, output reference clear and input XOR configuration and every extended HAL service (complementary outputs, break and dead time, commutation, Hall sensor, encoder index, dithering, ADC synchronisation, slave-mode preload, pulse on compare, input selection and remap); the LL advanced-control timer features (repetition counter, channels 5 and 6, complementary outputs, break, dead time, lock, off-states, output enable, commutation, second trigger output), encoder index and error detection, and the remaining LL options (update flag remap, dithering, output reference clear, pulse width, input XOR, external trigger source, slave-mode preload, ADC synchronisation, DMA burst, input remap).",
    "SWE.1 only, at the functional level: register-level detail and concrete negative cases belong to SWE.3."
  ],
